	(gr_text "JLCPCB production settings:\n\nAdditional settings after uploading the .zip gerber folder:\n\nPCB-Thickness: 1.2mm (I personally recommand staying between 1.2mm and 1.6mm)\nMaterial Type: FR4-TG155 (Important!)\nSurface finish: ENIG (Essential for these small pads)\nGold Thickness: 1 U{dblquote}\nMin via hole size/diameter: 0.3mm/(0.4/0.45mm)\n\nOptional settings you might want:\nPCB Color: Black (to your wish, I took black)\nMark on PCB: 2D barcode (Serial Number) (see picture below for my specs)\nInspection report: (Only add when you are actually interested, otherwise it costs you extra money for stuff you might not understand)\n\nIF YOU WANT TO ASSEMBLE THE PCB BY YOURSELF, BE ADVISED THAT THIS IS AN ADVANCED DESIGN AND EXPERTISE IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED!\n\nMy setup:\n- Bought all parts speratly from: Digikey, Mouser and LCSC\n- Bought PCB with Stencil\n- Buy an MHP50 on Amazon with an 100W USB-C Power Supply OR an old oven with a reflow controller\n- Add solder paste with a 3D-Printed hellper and the stencil on the PCB\n- Place all components (small to big), microskop is very helpful\n- reflow solder it\n\nStencil specs:\nStencil side: Top only\nDimensions: standard/Custom (Use what you like, I used a custom size of: 100mm * 100mm)\nPolishing Process: Electropolishing (Important!)"
		(at 13.85 166.95 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "f7f74247-3a30-4291-8e5c-b34b42568d38")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
